cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this material, please cite the deposited record and the accompanying article."
title: "Supplementary material and reproducibility package for \"Public Omics Data Reuse in Gastric Cancer: From Discovery Abundance to Translational Evidence\""
type: dataset
version: 1.0.0
license: CC-BY-4.0
abstract: >-
  Supplementary material and reproducibility package for a methodological narrative review on the
  reuse of public omics data in gastric cancer. Includes the complete PubMed search log, scan record
  counts, publication-trend dataset, the title/abstract reporting-signal screen of the 100 most
  recent prognostic-signature records with its coding rules, the public metadata scan, a
  full-text-verified comparison of the validation design of 11 representative prognostic-signature
  studies, a comparison of single-cell and spatial methods, the GC-PROVE practical appraisal
  checklist, and the generation scripts.
keywords:
  - gastric cancer
  - public omics data reuse
  - reproducibility
  - prognostic signature
  - data leakage
  - external validation
  - GC-PROVE
